IMPORT prelude

-- Geneva Conventions Act 1973 (Singapore) -- grave breaches of the scheduled Conventions and who may try them (s 3, with the lists in
-- First Schedule Art 50, Second Schedule Art 51, Third Schedule Art 130 and Fourth Schedule Art 147), the trial safeguards for
-- protected prisoners of war and internees (ss 4 to 7), and the ban on unauthorised use of the red cross and related emblems with its
-- penalty, inspectors and prosecution consent (ss 8 to 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GCA1973.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 40 of 2019 (Supreme Court of Judicature (Amendment) Act 2019, in s 6(2), commenced 2 January 2021).
-- Part IV is omitted from the deposit "as having had its effect".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0127 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. For an ordinary person or business the answer is mostly Part 3 (the emblems); Part 2 is encoded because it is the
-- rest of the operative Act and is short. Not encoded: the text of the four Conventions and the Fifth Schedule Protocol beyond the
-- four grave-breach lists; the Minister's certificate under s 3(4) on whether a Convention applies (Article 2); s 3(5) on subordinate
-- military courts; the particulars a s 4 notice must contain (s 4(2)) and proof of service (s 4(3)); the assignment and payment of
-- counsel (s 5(3), (4)); the investigative powers of inspectors (s 10A(2), (3)) beyond the offence in s 10A(4); the drawings in the
-- Sixth Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Geneva Conventions Act 1973 -- grave breaches, protected persons on trial, emblems`

DECLARE Convention IS ONE OF
    `the First Schedule Convention (wounded and sick in the field)`
    `the Second Schedule Convention (wounded, sick and shipwrecked at sea)`
    `the Third Schedule Convention (prisoners of war)`
    `the Fourth Schedule Convention (civilians)`

DECLARE `Act against protected persons or property` IS ONE OF
    `wilful killing`
    `torture or inhuman treatment`
    `wilfully causing great suffering or serious injury`
    `extensive unjustified destruction or appropriation of property`
    `compelling service in the forces of a hostile Power`
    `wilfully depriving of a fair and regular trial`
    `unlawful deportation, transfer or confinement`
    `taking of hostages`
    `petty theft from a protected person`

DECLARE `Section 3 maximum` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for life`
    `imprisonment up to 14 years`
    `no offence under section 3`

DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `the High Court`
    `a District Court`
    `a Magistrate's Court`

DECLARE Accused IS ONE OF
    `a protected prisoner of war`
    `a protected internee`
    `any other accused person`

§§ `3 -- grave breaches`

-- s 3(1): "Any person, whatever his or her citizenship or nationality, who, whether in or outside Singapore, commits, aids, abets or
-- procures the commission by any other person of any grave breach" mentioned in First Schedule Art 50, Second Schedule Art 51, Third
-- Schedule Art 130 or Fourth Schedule Art 147, is guilty of an offence: (e) "involving the wilful killing of a person protected by the
-- Convention in question, to imprisonment for life"; (f) any other grave breach, "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years".
-- The Articles (each "if committed against persons or property protected by the Convention"):
--   Art 50 (First) and Art 51 (Second): wilful killing, torture or inhuman treatment, wilfully causing great suffering or serious
--     injury, "extensive destruction and appropriation of property, not justified by military necessity and carried out unlawfully
--     and wantonly".
--   Art 130 (Third): wilful killing, torture or inhuman treatment, great suffering, "compelling a prisoner of war to serve in the
--     forces of the hostile Power", "wilfully depriving a prisoner of war of the rights of fair and regular trial". No property item.
--   Art 147 (Fourth): all of the above, plus "unlawful deportation or transfer or unlawful confinement of a protected person" and
--     "taking of hostages".
-- Citizenship, nationality and place are irrelevant by the words of s 3(1); they are therefore not inputs here.
GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Act against protected persons or property`, `the convention` IS A Convention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a grave breach of the convention` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `wilful killing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `torture or inhuman treatment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wilfully causing great suffering or serious injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `extensive unjustified destruction or appropriation of property` THEN
        CONSIDER `the convention`
        WHEN `the Third Schedule Convention (prisoners of war)` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `compelling service in the forces of a hostile Power` THEN
        CONSIDER `the convention`
        WHEN `the Third Schedule Convention (prisoners of war)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Fourth Schedule Convention (civilians)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `wilfully depriving of a fair and regular trial` THEN
        CONSIDER `the convention`
        WHEN `the Third Schedule Convention (prisoners of war)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Fourth Schedule Convention (civilians)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `unlawful deportation, transfer or confinement` THEN
        CONSIDER `the convention`
        WHEN `the Fourth Schedule Convention (civilians)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `taking of hostages` THEN
        CONSIDER `the convention`
        WHEN `the Fourth Schedule Convention (civilians)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Act against protected persons or property`, `the convention` IS A Convention,
      `the victim is protected by that Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an offence under section 3` IF
    `the act is a grave breach of the convention` `the act` `the convention` AND `the victim is protected by that Convention`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Act against protected persons or property`, `the convention` IS A Convention,
      `the victim is protected by that Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 3 maximum`
DECIDE `the section 3 maximum sentence` IS
    IF NOT `the act is an offence under section 3` `the act` `the convention` `the victim is protected by that Convention`
    THEN `no offence under section 3`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the act`
         WHEN `wilful killing` THEN `imprisonment for life`
         OTHERWISE `imprisonment up to 14 years`

-- s 3(3): "No Magistrate's Court or District Court has jurisdiction to try any offence under this section, and proceedings for the
-- offence must not be instituted except by or on behalf of the Public Prosecutor." (s 3(2): an offence outside Singapore may be tried
-- "in any place in Singapore as if the offence had been committed in that place".)
GIVEN `the trial court` IS A Court, `instituted by or on behalf of the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may try a section 3 offence` IF
    `instituted by or on behalf of the Public Prosecutor` AND
        CONSIDER `the trial court`
        WHEN `the High Court` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- notice of trial to the Protecting Power`

-- s 4(1): the court before which "(a) a protected prisoner of war is brought up for trial for any offence; or (b) a protected internee is
-- brought up for trial for an offence for which that court has power to sentence him or her to death or to imprisonment for a term of
-- 2 years or more, must not proceed with the trial until it is proved ... that a notice ... has been served not less than 3 weeks
-- previously on the Protecting Power" (and, for a prisoner of war, on the accused and the prisoner's representative). 3 weeks is
-- taken as 21 days. (5): the court may remand the accused for an adjournment to comply.
GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `the court may sentence to death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court's maximum imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 4 notice is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the accused`
    WHEN `a protected prisoner of war` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a protected internee` THEN `the court may sentence to death` OR (`the court's maximum imprisonment in years` AT LEAST 2)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `the court may sentence to death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court's maximum imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `days since the notice was served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trial may proceed under section 4` IF
        (NOT `a section 4 notice is required` `the accused` `the court may sentence to death` `the court's maximum imprisonment in years`)
    OR  (`days since the notice was served` AT LEAST 21)

§§ `5 -- legal representation`

-- s 5(1): the court before which "(a) any person is brought up for trial for an offence under section 3; or (b) a protected prisoner of
-- war is brought up for trial for any offence, shall not proceed with the trial unless (c) the accused is represented by counsel; and
-- (d) ... a period of at least 14 days has elapsed since instructions for the representation of the accused at the trial were first
-- given to the counsel". (2), (3): counsel instructed by the Protecting Power, or assigned by the court, counts as representing the
-- accused, "without affecting the requirements of subsection (1)(d)".
GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `charged under section 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 applies to the trial` IF
        `charged under section 3`
    OR  CONSIDER `the accused`
        WHEN `a protected prisoner of war` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `charged under section 3` IS A BOOLEAN, `represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since counsel was first instructed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trial may proceed under section 5` IF
        (NOT `section 5 applies to the trial` `the accused` `charged under section 3`)
    OR  (`represented by counsel` AND (`days since counsel was first instructed` AT LEAST 14))

§§ `6 -- appeals by protected persons`

-- s 6(1): "A protected prisoner of war or a protected internee who has been convicted and sentenced to death or to imprisonment for a
-- term of 2 years or more may appeal against the conviction and sentence". (2): "Despite section 377(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code
-- 2010, notice of an appeal ... shall be given not later than 10 days after the date on which the protected person receives a notice"
-- (from an SAF officer, or for an internee from the prison governor) "that the Protecting Power has been notified of the protected
-- person's conviction and sentence". [40/2019]
GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `sentenced to death` IS A BOOLEAN, `sentenced imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a section 6 appeal` IF
    (`sentenced to death` OR (`sentenced imprisonment in years` AT LEAST 2)) AND
        CONSIDER `the accused`
        WHEN `a protected prisoner of war` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a protected internee` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `days after receiving notice that the Protecting Power was notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 6 appeal notice is in time` IF
    `days after receiving notice that the Protecting Power was notified` AT MOST 10

§§ `7 -- powers of the Minister`

-- s 7(1): where a protected prisoner of war or protected internee is sentenced to imprisonment, the Minister may direct a deduction of
-- "a period not exceeding the period (if any) during which that person was in custody in connection with that offence, either on remand
-- or after committal for trial (including the period of the trial)". (2): where a protected prisoner of war "has been in custody ... for
-- an aggregate period of at least 3 months", the Minister may direct transfer to the custody of an SAF officer.
GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `days in custody before sentence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most the Minister may deduct in days` IS
    CONSIDER `the accused`
    WHEN `a protected prisoner of war` THEN `days in custody before sentence`
    WHEN `a protected internee` THEN `days in custody before sentence`
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused, `aggregate months in custody` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may transfer to military custody` IF
    (`aggregate months in custody` AT LEAST 3) AND
        CONSIDER `the accused`
        WHEN `a protected prisoner of war` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8, 9 -- the emblems`

-- s 8: "A person must not, without the Minister's authority, use for any purpose in Singapore" (a) the red crescent emblem; (b) the red
-- cross emblem; (c) the red crystal emblem; (d) the red lion and sun emblem; or (e) "the words 'Red Cross' or 'Geneva Cross'".
-- s 9: "A person must not, without the Minister's authority, use for any purpose whatsoever" (a) "any design consisting of a white or
-- silver cross on a red ground, none of the limbs of which extends to the margin of the ground, being the cross comprised in the Arms of
-- the Swiss Confederation"; (b) a colourable imitation of (a); (c) a colourable imitation of any of the four emblems; (d) "any words so
-- nearly resembling the words 'Red Cross' or 'Geneva Cross' as to be capable of being understood as referring to the red cross emblem".
-- s 8 is limited to use "in Singapore"; s 9 carries no such words. Read literally, s 9 reaches use anywhere. That is the reading
-- encoded; whether a court would read a territorial limit into s 9 is an open question (inference, not in the text).
-- The blue "star of life" is not in either list and is not, on its face, an imitation of any listed mark (inference).
DECLARE Mark IS ONE OF
    `the red cross emblem`
    `the red crescent emblem`
    `the red crystal emblem`
    `the red lion and sun emblem`
    `the words Red Cross`
    `the words Geneva Cross`
    `the Swiss Arms white cross on red`
    `a colourable imitation of the Swiss Arms cross`
    `a colourable imitation of one of the four emblems`
    `words so nearly resembling Red Cross as to refer to the emblem`
    `a blue star of life`

GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark, `used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the Minister's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is prohibited by section 8` IF
    `used in Singapore` AND (NOT `with the Minister's authority`) AND
        CONSIDER `the mark`
        WHEN `the red cross emblem` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the red crescent emblem` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the red crystal emblem` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the red lion and sun emblem` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the words Red Cross` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the words Geneva Cross` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark, `with the Minister's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is prohibited by section 9` IF
    (NOT `with the Minister's authority`) AND
        CONSIDER `the mark`
        WHEN `the Swiss Arms white cross on red` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a colourable imitation of the Swiss Arms cross` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a colourable imitation of one of the four emblems` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `words so nearly resembling Red Cross as to refer to the emblem` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark, `used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the Minister's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 10` IF
        `the use is prohibited by section 8` `the mark` `used in Singapore` `with the Minister's authority`
    OR  `the use is prohibited by section 9` `the mark` `with the Minister's authority`

§§ `10, 10A, 11 -- penalty, inspectors, prosecution`

-- s 10(1): contravening Part 3 -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both and, in
-- addition, any goods upon or in connection with which the emblem, design or words ... was or were used, shall be forfeited". [55/2007]
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 10 maximum fine in dollars` IS 10000

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 10 maximum imprisonment in months` IS 6

GIVEN `convicted under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods bearing the mark are forfeited` IF `convicted under section 10`

-- s 10(2): where an offence by "a body corporate or society is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of any
-- director, manager, secretary or other officer", that officer, "as well as the body corporate or society", is deemed guilty.
GIVEN `the body corporate or society committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body corporate or society committed the offence` AND `the officer consented or connived`

-- s 10A(4): any person who, "without lawful excuse", (a) refuses to answer an inspector or gives a false answer, (b) refuses or fails to
-- comply with a requirement under (2), or (c) wilfully obstructs an inspector, is liable to "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both". [55/2007]
GIVEN `refused, answered falsely, failed to comply or wilfully obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct towards the inspector is an offence` IF
    `refused, answered falsely, failed to comply or wilfully obstructed` AND (NOT `had a lawful excuse`)

-- s 11: "Proceedings under this Part must not be instituted without the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3 proceedings may be instituted` IF `the Public Prosecutor consented`
